        "id": "p21-q9-root",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "I think of a number and divide it by 5. The answer is 4. What is the number?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{x}{5}=4$; the number is $20$.",
          "worked": "Let $x$ be the number.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{x}{5}&=4\\\\\\frac{x}{5}\\times5&=4\\times5\\\\x&=20\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe number is $20$. Check: $20\\div5=4$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 46
      },
      {
        "id": "p21-q10-root",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "In 29 years’ time a man will reach the retiring age of 65 years. How old is he now?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x+29=65$; the man is $36$ years old.",
          "worked": "Let $x$ be the man's present age in years.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}x+29&=65\\\\x+29-29&=65-29\\\\x&=36\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe man is $36$ years old. Check: $36+29=65$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      }
    ]
